From f6297a99f07d7045d42f46e1a915721217228638 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:19:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve Cargo dependency aliases in Bazel Rust targets

Restrict alias labels to each target's normal, development, or build
 dependencies and preserve platform conditions. This avoids introducing
 development-only dependency cycles into ordinary library builds.

Include an integration regression that uses the maintained YAML parser
 through its serde_yaml alias and verifies the public skill metadata.

Base: rust-v0.162.1 (092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d).
Prerequisite for the renamed-parser regression: maintained-yaml-parser.patch.

Red: bazel test //codex-rs/skills:skills-yaml_dependency_alias-test
 without the macro repair fails E0433 resolving serde_yaml. Evidence:
 final-queue-verification-z5VhEx/yaml-alias-regression-red.log.
Green: the regression and skills-unit-tests pass with scoped aliases.
 Evidence: yaml-alias-regression-green.log. just fmt-check passes:
 yaml-alias-format.log. Fresh emitted acceptance remains required.
